															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/darkstuff" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1581620); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1581620&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607950783" alt="DarkStuff" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1581620)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/darkstuff" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1581620); return false;" >DarkStuff</a></span> <span class="odate time_1508472133 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Oct 2017 04:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3616721">
									

<p>So, theories. This gal seems to be a anartist of the performing arts. This time they got a gig with a big&#8230; pony, thing. Run by Pink. Anyways, as shown in&#8230; ah fuck, I don't know what the tales are called. Probably made by Scantron, the GAW ones where they're running from the Foundation. Anyways, the side character talks weirdly.</p>
<p>When asked, Scantron(?) said that its because working with the anomalous fucks with your brain. So he said that the reason this guy talks all jittery is because he works by cutting things up and pasting them together in anomalous fashions. Thus, his speech is very &quot;cut up and pasted back together&quot;, forming weird sentence structure and repeating words. I think the same thing is happening to the main character here.</p>
<p>She creates art in some dream like fashion. Or maybe with drugs. Or maybe both. But I feel that her works of art work like a dream journal: she'll wake up in the middle of the night (or be in the middle of a high) and an idea will come to her head and she'll write it down. And the works of art she creates are anomalous. This fucks with her head,the same way that Scantron(?) described in his articles. If she makes dream like things, eventually her whole world becomes more dreamlike.</p>
<p>What we are reading here is the world as she sees it: senseless and shifting and scary. Why can she fly? Who are these people? What is she doing? Even she doesn't know, the Moeller twins pretty much keep her around for shits and giggles (and maybe they were friends once, when she was still able to keep her head straight). We are seeing someone who delved too deep into anart. Someone whose mind is completely lost to the anomalous influences both internal and external.</p>
<p>That's how I read it, anyways.</p>
<p>EDIT: <em>Oh, I forgot an integral part of this theory. &quot;Sometimes you make mistakes, and sometimes mistakes make you.&quot; The main character here is an example of when your mistakes make you. Her mistakes in anart and possibly drugs are what make her world one of constant mindfuckery and nonsense. In my interpretation, this is the Foundation's equivalent of a cautionary tale.</em></p>
<p>EDIT 2: <em>It</em> was <em>Scantron, and the character's name was Armand. Here's the link to the beginning of the tale series: <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-assassination-of-beleaguered-normalcy-by-the-coward-game">http://www.scp-wiki.net/the-assassination-of-beleaguered-normalcy-by-the-coward-game</a> if you want it.</em></p>

							</div>

								
